  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "This is revenue.",
      "pair": "p1",
      "show": "left",
      "react": "point-up-left",
      "sfx": [
        "pop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "And this is profit.",
      "pair": "p1",
      "show": "right",
      "react": "point-up-right",
      "sfx": [
        "pop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "But what's the difference?",
      "pair": "p1",
      "react": "thinking",
      "question": true,
      "sfx": [
        "question"
      ],
      "pause": 0.5
    },
    {
      "text": "Revenue is the total money a business earns from selling products or services.",
      "pair": "p1",
      "focus": "left",
      "react": "point-up-left",
      "sfx": [
        "pop"
      ],
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "pop",
          "el": "#rev-products",
          "word": "products",
          "sfx": "coin"
        },
        {
          "type": "pop",
          "el": "#rev-services",
          "word": "services.",
          "sfx": "coin"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Profit is what's left after subtracting expenses.",
      "pair": "p1",
      "focus": "right",
      "react": "point-up-right",
      "sfx": [
        "pop"
      ],
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "pop",
          "el": "#pr-exp",
          "word": "subtracting",
          "sfx": "minus"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For example, if a business earns $10,000 and spends $7,000, its profit is $3,000.",
      "pair": "p1",
      "react": "smirk-thumb",
      "pause": 0.55,
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "pulse",
          "el": "#rev-total",
          "word": "$10,000"
        },
        {
          "type": "pulse",
          "el": "#pr-exp",
          "word": "$7,000,"
        },
        {
          "type": "swap",
          "from": "#pr-old",
          "to": "#pr-new",
          "word": "$3,000.",
          "sfx": "reward"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Now, what about assets and liabilities?",
      "pair": "p2",
      "react": "look-up",
      "question": true,
      "sfx": [
        "question"
      ],
      "pause": 0.5
    },
    {
      "text": "Assets are valuable things a business owns, like cash, buildings, and equipment.",
      "pair": "p2",
      "focus": "left",
      "react": "point-up-left",
      "sfx": [
        "pop"
      ],
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "pop",
          "el": "#as-cash",
          "word": "cash,",
          "sfx": "add"
        },
        {
          "type": "pop",
          "el": "#as-building",
          "word": "buildings,",
          "sfx": "add"
        },
        {
          "type": "pop",
          "el": "#as-equip",
          "word": "equipment.",
          "sfx": "add"
        },
        {
          "type": "pop",
          "el": "#as-total",
          "word": "equipment.",
          "delay": 0.45
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Liabilities are what a business owes, like loans, unpaid bills, and debts.",
      "pair": "p2",
      "focus": "right",
      "react": "point-up-right",
      "sfx": [
        "pop"
